# A creature that enters attacking was never declared as an attacker, so "whenever a creature attacks" does not see it
# (CR 508.4, 702.190b; the ruling). Bot1 has Curse of Predation on Bot2 ("whenever a creature attacks enchanted player, put a
# +1/+1 counter on it"). The Ornithopter that attacks Bot2 gets its counter (the positive control); Leonardo, sneaked in for
# {W} in its place and attacking Bot2, gets none from the Curse: he deals 1, not 2 (Bot2 at 19), and his only counter is the
# one his own lifelink gain gives him.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Plains
Ornithopter
Curse of Predation
Leonardo, Cutting Edge
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Curse of Predation.Cast(Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Hand.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Cast(Ability: Sneak)
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Combat.Attackers = Leonardo, Cutting Edge > Bot2
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Life = 21
Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Power = 2
